.\" Manpage for iris-apply-settings, part of the iris-theme package.
.TH IRIS-APPLY-SETTINGS 1 "October 2026" "iris-theme" "Iris desktop skin"
.SH NAME
iris-apply-settings \- apply a validated Iris GSettings profile to a user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iris-apply-settings
.RI [ profile ]
.RI [ \-\-user\ NAME ]
.RI [ \-\-dry-run ]
.RI [ \-\-restore\ FILE ]
.RI [ \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IR iris-apply-settings
reads a profile file of
.IR schema key value
lines and writes each value with
.BR gsettings (1),
after checking the schema and key against the schemas that are actually
installed on this machine.
.PP
This is deliberately not a
.BR "dconf load"
front end. A
.IR dconf
dump writes every key it contains, including keys that no application defines
any more, and it replaces a whole subtree without recording what was there
before. Here a line naming an unknown schema or key is skipped with a warning,
the previous value of every key that is changed is saved first, and the result
is a file that can be replayed or reversed.
.PP
It must be run from inside a live graphical session: it needs the user's
D-Bus session bus and refuses to run (rather than writing to a wrong or empty
database) when that bus is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "profile"
Path to the profile. Defaults to
.IR /usr/share/iris/config/gsettings/iris.gsettings ,
which is the profile shipped by this package.
.TP
.BI "\-\-user " NAME
Apply the profile as
.IR NAME
instead of the invoking user. When run under
.BR sudo ,
the invoking user is taken from
.IR SUDO_USER .
.TP
.BI "\-\-dry-run"
Report what would be written and what would be skipped. Nothing is written, no
backup is created.
.TP
.BI "\-\-restore " FILE
Replay a backup file created by an earlier run, restoring the values the key
had before Iris changed them. The file lives under
.IR ~/.local/share/iris/settings-backup/ .
.TP
.BI "\-\-yes , " \-y
Do not ask for confirmation before writing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when the profile was applied (or every remaining line was
deliberately skipped with a warning), and non-zero when the profile is
unreadable, the session bus is missing, or
.BR gsettings (1)
rejected a value.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/iris/config/gsettings/iris.gsettings
The shipped profile: panel layout and height, applet placement, window and
notification behaviour. Lines starting with
.B #
are comments; every other line is
.IR "schema<TAB>key<TAB>value" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/iris/settings-backup/
Timestamped backups of previous values, one file per run, used by
.BR \-\-restore .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR dconf (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/iris-theme/README.md
